rnon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":44,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Australian Medical Council\nHandbook of Multiple Choice Questions","options":{"A":"Diagnostically more sensitive in premenopausal than in postmenopausal women,","B":"More likely than self-examination to detect early cancers.","C":"The investigation most able to differentiate cystic from solid lesions.","D":"Painless.","E":"Most useful in women who have a palpable breast lump.\n\nExample\nMCQ 1.18 — ATTEMPTED SUICIDE - CARBON MONOXIDE POISONING\n\nA 28-year-old man has been brought by ambulance to the Emergency Department\nafter being found unconscious in his 25-year-old car. A hose pipe was found\nconnecting the exhaust to the interior of the car, with the engine running, when he\nwas discovered by his wife in their garage. His carboxyhaemoglobin level was 40%\non admission. Which one of the following is the least likely consequence of his carbon\nmonoxide posioning?\n\nDelirium (acute brain syndrome).\n\nDementia (chronic brain syndrome).\n\n. Hydrocephalus.\n\nExtrapyramidal signs.\n\nGood recovery.\n\nMOQOR>\n\nExample\nMCQ 1.19 —- PANIC ATTACKS - EPIDEMIOLOGY\n\nConcerning panic attacks, each of the following clinical features is"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"low","currentness_keywords":[],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"1162bc9b58150ae7b6c61d4a6c30e8b946e0aad9","duplicate_group_id":"exact-1162bc9b5815","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"b1c940ae9d5a17bcddaa","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice 