A 15-year-old girl presents with a three-day history of persistent severe vomiting
associated with an intercurrent viral infection. She has been complaining of tiredness
and lack of energy for the previous three to four months. On examination she has
a BP of 80/50mmbg, pulse 130/min and has increased pigmentation of her buccal
mucosa and nipples. Urinalysis is normal. Her serum sodium is 118mmol/L (135-145)
and her serum chloride is 76mmol/L (95-110). Which one of the following is the most
likely cause for her presentation?','{"A":"Addison disease.","B":"Salt-losing congenital adrenal hyperplasia.","C":"‘Chronic fatigue syndrome’ (CFS).","D":"Chronic reflux nephropathy.","E":"Hyperthyroid crisis.\n\nMCQ 2.005\n\nA 3-year-old girl has frequent episodic asthma and persistent interval symptoms\nof nocturnal cough and exercise-induced wheezing. Which one of the following\ndelivery methods would be most appropriate to administer fluticasone effectively to\nthis child?\n\nA. Nebuliser and pump.\n\nB. Breath-actuated inhaler (Accuhaler®).\nC. Metered dose inhaler (MDI).\n\nD. MDI and spacer device with mask.\n\nE. Oral suspension.\n\nMCQ 2.006\n\nA mother brings in her 3-month-old infant daughter, saying she has noted difficulty\nin applying nappies. Birth was by vaginal delivery of a breech presentation with\nextended legs. The baby is otherwise well. On examination, you note limited\nabduction of one hip. Which one of the following additional clinical findings is\nlikely to be most helpful in confirming the diagnosis of developmental dysplasia\n(congenital dislocation) of the hip?\n\n. Asymmetry of groin crease lines.\nInequality of leg length.\n\n. A ‘clicking’ hip on extension.\n\n. A ‘jerk’ while abducting the flexed hip.\nInternal femoral version of the hip.\n\nalte) (O) e-) o>"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"2.004","duplicate_group_id":"exact-36ebf2aed7e4","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"dfda30704bb67db7eea6","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":63,"source_qid":"2.004"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verif