Section 2 = Trial Examination
MCQ 2.013
An 80-year-old woman presented /
with a 24-hour history of a painful |
tender swelling under the right
side of the jaw associated with a
tender swelling under the tongue. }
The illustration shows the intraoral
appearance. In order to confirm
the diagnosis, which one of the
following would be the most
appropriate investigation?','{"A":"Intraoral plain radiograph.","B":"Ultrasound focused on the\nregion below the jaw.","C":"Computed tomogram (CT) of the head and neck.","D":"Sialogram of the submandibular salivary duct.","E":"Magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) of the head and neck.\n\nMCQ 2.014\n\nA 61-year-old Asian man seeks advice on his risk of developing carcinoma of the\nprostate. He has no symptoms suggestive of bladder neck outflow obstruction, is i\ngood health and does not take any medications. He stopped smoking 10 years ago\nwith a 30 pack-year history, and is retired from the aniline dye industry. His fathe\ndeveloped carcinoma of the prostate at the age of 58. Which one of the following\nis the most important risk factor for this man?\n\nHis ethnic origins.\n\nHis age.\n\n. His family history.\n\nHis past history of smoking.\nHis work in the dye industry.\n\nMOQOR>\n\nMCQ 2.015\n\nA 27-year-old man with a history of heroin dependence presents to the Emergeni\nDepartment with abdominal pain and vomiting. He appears agitated in mood, and\nhas tachycardia and fever and dilated pupils. He admits recent use of cocaine and\nheroin. Which one of the following clinical findings is most helpful in differentiating\ncocaine intoxication from heroin withdrawal?\n\n. Agitation.\n\nAbdominal pain and vomiting.\n. Tachycardia.\n. Dilated pupils.\n\nFever.\n\nnm OQ 2 >"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"2.013","duplicate_group_id":"exact-8dacb6880640","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"e0710734e43fa5031767","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":66,"source_qid":"2.013"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','low','{"record_id":"e0710734e43fa5031767","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":66,"source_qid":"2.013","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Australian Medical Council\nSection 2 = Trial Examination\nMCQ 2.013\nAn 80-year-old woman presented /\nwith a 24-hour history of a painful |\ntender swelling under the right\nside of the jaw associated with a\ntender swelling under the tongue. }\nThe illustration shows the intraoral\nappearance. In order to confirm\nthe diagnosis, which one of the\nfollowing would be the most\nappropriate investigation?","options":{"A":"Intraoral plain radiograph.","B":"Ultrasound focused on the\nregion below the jaw.","C":"Computed tomogram (CT) of the head and neck.","D":"Sialogram of the submandibular salivary duct.","E":"Magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) of the head and neck.\n\nMCQ 2.014\n\nA 61-year-old Asian man seeks advice on his risk of developing carcinoma of the\nprostate. He has no symptoms suggestive of bladder neck outflow obstruction, is i\ngood health and does not take any medications. He stopped smoking 10 years ago\nwith a 30 pack-year history, and is retired from the aniline dye industry. His fathe\ndeveloped carcinoma of the prostate at the age of 58. Which one of the following\nis the most important risk factor for this man?\n\nHis ethnic origins.\n\nHis age.\n\n. His family history.\n\nHis past history of smoking.\nHis work in the dye industry.\n\nMOQOR>\n\nMCQ 2.015\n\nA 27-year-old man with a history of heroin dependence presents to the Emergeni\nDepartment with abdominal pain and vomiting. He appears agitated in mood, and\nhas tachycardia and fever and dilated pupils. He admits recent use of cocaine and\nheroin. Which one of the following clinical findings is most helpful in differentiating\ncocaine intoxication from heroin withdrawal?\n\n. Agitation.\n\nAbdominal pain and vomiting.\n. Tachycardia.\n. Dilated pupils.\n\nFever.\n\nnm OQ 2 >"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"low","currentness_keywords":[],"likely_visual_question":true,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"8dacb68806402a5cd9709338c625befd5d89dd82","duplicate_group_id":"exact-8dacb6880640","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"e0710734e43fa5031767","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":66,"source_qid":"2.013"}]}',0,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,visual_asset=excluded.visual_asset,visual_url=excluded.visual_url,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk,record_json=excluded.record_json,active_quiz=excluded.active_quiz,import_version=excluded.import_version,imported_at=excluded.imported_at;
