MCQ 2.028
A 20-year-old woman presents with hypertension. She has a previous history of
enuresis and febrile episodes in childhood. Which one of the following is the most
likely diagnosis from this history?','{"A":"Chronic glomerulonephritis.","B":"Reflux nephropathy.","C":"Essential hypertension.","D":"Polycystic disease of the kidneys.","E":"Analgesic nephropathy.\n\nMCQ 2.029\n\nA 23-year-old man_ is transferred to the\nEmergency Department following a demolition\nsite accident in which a beam fell on him and\npinned him by the chest. He has a clear airway\nand is able to speak to you in gasps. His BP is\n110/75mmHg and pulse rate is 105/min. Air entry\nis diminished over the right side of the chest,\nwith a small area of subcutaneous emphysema\npalpable posteriorly. Computed tomography\n(CT) shows he has bilateral rib fractures from the\ntight second through to the seventh ribs with a\nsmall haemopneumothorax on the right as illustrated. After the scan his breathing\nbecomes more laboured and he shows signs of paradoxical respiration of chest wall\nretraction during inspiration. Which one of the following is the most appropriate initial\naction to take in his management?\n\n. Strap the chest.\nInsert a right-sided pleural underwater-sealed drain.\n\n. Aspirate the right pneumothorax.\n\n. Institute positive-pressure ventilation via an endotracheal tube.\nAdminister bilateral intercostal blocks for analgesia.\n\nee SS Ss SRS SSS SS\n\nMCQ 2.030\n\nA mother brings her 2-year-old son to the clinic. She is concerned that her child\nhas stopped growing. The child is on the 50th percentile for height and weight and\nprevious records show he has remained on this growth curve for height and weight.\nYou notice that his height has not changed from three months ago. Which one of\nthe following is the most appropriate next step in management?\n\npu WS) () We Bem\n\nA. Reassure the mother and review in three months.\n\nB. Order growth hormone studies.\n\nC. Order bone films of the hand and wrist.\n\nD. Order thyroid studies.\n\nE. Advise the mother to increase the child’s calorie intake."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of 