mo.
MCQ 2.044
An 18-year-old woman has maintained a body mass index (BMI) of 13 after years of
food restriction and an obsessional daily exercise routine. She has attended the clinic
coincidentally for management of a whiplash injury after a car accident. Which one
of the following is most likely to be found on general physical examination of this
young woman?
. Tachycardia.
Low grade pyrexia.
. Delayed relaxation phase of the ankle jerk.
Shivering in a cool environment.
Loss of breast development.
TTMOQOR>
MCQ 2.045
An 85-year-old man has a history of intermittent lower abdominal pain, diarrhoea
and recurrent lower urinary tract infections with coliform organisms. He now presen
with a history of noticing bubbling in the urinary stream, with ‘whistling down mi
pipe’. Which one of the following is the most likely underlying cause of his problem?','{"A":"Diverticular disease of the colon.","B":"A carcinoma of the bladder.","C":"Acarcinoma of the sigmoid colon.","D":"Pneumatosis cystoides intestinalis.","E":"A urachal cyst.\n\nee\n\nMCQ 2.046\n\nA 45-year-old man presents with a six-month history of increasing weakness of his.\ntight arm and right leg. Over the last two months he has had headaches, which\nare gradually getting more severe. The patient reports that over the last five years\nhe has had a number of ‘blackouts’, which were associated with incontinence for\nwhich he did not seek medical advice. On examination he has weakness of the 4\nright upper and lower limbs. The only other abnormal finding is papilloedema. Which We\none of the following would best explain this clinical picture?\n\nA left frontal glioblastoma multiforme.\nSagittal sinus thrombosis.\n\n. Acerebral abscess.\n\n. A left-sided cerebral haemorrhage.\n\nA left frontal meningioma.\n\n—— —\n\nEUS): U2: 3"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"2.044","duplicate_group_id":"exact-1738681bd6c9","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"f1c29923cb0eff538810","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":76,"source_qid":"2.044"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"f1c29923cb0eff538810","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":76,"source_qid":"