ternal grandmother also\nhad breast cancer before the age of 50. The patient is on the oral contraceptive\npill (OCP) and no other medications; her general health is normal. Mammography\nis normal. An ultrasound of the breasts shows an uncomplicated cyst with no\nconcerning features in the right breast. Apart from advice about use of simple\nanalgesics and evening primrose oil for her mastalgia, which one of the following is\nthe most appropriate advice in the patient''s followup regimen?\n\nA. Cease the OCP, yearly clinical review, yearly mammography and ultrasound.\n\nB. Remain on the OCP, yearly clinical review, yearly mammography and\nultrasound.\n\nC. Remain on the OCP, six-monthly clinical review, yearly mammography and\nultrasound.\n\nD. Remain on the OCP, two-yearly clinical and mammography review.\n\nE. Cease the OCP, yearly clinical and ultrasound review.\n\nMCQ 2.049\n\nA 31-year-old man is treated with triple therapy (a proton pump inhibitor and two\nantibiotics) for an endoscopically proven duodenal ulcer. He has tested positive for\nHelicobacter pylori. After 10 days of treatment he has improved but is not yet fully\nsymptom-free. Which one of the following is the most appropriate followup for the\npatient?\n\nSerum gastrin estimation.\n\nUrea breath test at six weeks.\n\n. Repeat endoscopy at four weeks.\n\nSerology for H. pylori antibodies at two months.\n\nRepeat endoscopy at two months.\n\nMOQS>"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"low","currentness_keywords":[],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"38e6638f2dea4616ea501ca053e1d01943fe1d9f","duplicate_group_id":"exact-38e6638f2dea","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"0101a8b9fda9288822d6","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":77,"source_qid":"2.047"}]}',0,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,visual_asset=excluded.visual_asset,visual_url=excluded.visual_url,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk,record_json=excluded.record_json,active_quiz=excluded.active_quiz,import_version=excluded.import_version,imported_at=excluded.imported_at;
