Section 2 = Trial Examination
MCQ 2.070
A 16-year-old girl is brought to the Emergency Department by her mother. Thé
girl complains of persistent dull right-sided lower abdominal pain which has beef
recently increasing in severity. She also has spotting of blood per vaginam. Her lag
normal period was seven weeks ago. The mother informs you that her daughter ha
not been sexually active. On examination, the daughter looks unwell and is sweating
with clammy cold skin, her temperature is 36.5°C, BP 80/50mmHg and pulse 140/mi
The lower abdomen shows rebound tenderness and guarding in the right iliac fossa
Which one of the following is the most appropriate immediate next step in her care?
. Speak privately to the daughter about her sexual activity.
Perform a vaginal pelvic examination.
. Commence intravenous fluid resuscitation.
. Perform urinary beta-hCG pregnancy test.
Arrange for urgent transvaginal ultrasound.
MOQ >
MCQ 2.071
After his baby sister was born, a é-year-old boy began sucking his thumb and
wetting his bed, behaviours he had ‘grown out of'' long before. His behaviour is a
example of which one of the following?
Reaction formation.
Regression.
. Acting out.
. Jealousy.
Compensation.
MOOR >
MCQ 2.072
This is the photograph of a 17-year-old girl. The swelling
visible in her neck has been present for several months,
is painless and is slowly increasing in size. She has not
noticed any voice changes, nor has she experienced
any difficulty in swallowing or breathing. The lump is not
attached to the overlying skin and moves on swallowing.
Which one of the following is the most likely diagnosis?','{"A":"Medullary carcinoma of the thyroid.","B":"Thyroglossal duct cyst.","C":"Papillary carcinoma of the thyroid.","D":"Branchial cyst.","E":"Colloid cyst confined to the thyroid isthmus.\n\nSUE\nMCQ 2.073\n\nA 26-year-old woman (gravida 3, para 2), whose only Papanicolaou (Pap) smear\ntest was done five years ago and was normal, is admitted to hospital at 33 weeks of\ngestation, following an antepartum haemorrhage of 300mL. The bleeding has now\nceased. Vital signs are as follows."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"2.070","duplicate_group_id":"exact-b97376d51166","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"1a756fa7789fda47c756","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":84,"source_qid":"2.070"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"1a756fa7789fda47c756","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":84,"source_qid":"2.070","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Ausiralian Medical Council\nSection 2 = Trial Examination\nMCQ 2.070\nA 16-year-old girl is brought to the Emergency Department by her mother. Thé\ngirl complains of persistent dull right-sided lower abdominal pain which has beef\nrecently increasing in severity. She also has spotting of blood per vaginam. Her lag\nnormal period was seven weeks ago. The mother informs you that her daughter ha\nnot been sexually active. On examination, the daughter looks unwell and is sweating\nwith clammy cold skin, her temperature is 36.5°C, BP 80/50mmHg and pulse 140/mi\nThe lower abdomen shows rebound tenderness and guarding in the right iliac fossa\nWhich one of the following is the most appropriate immediate next step in her care?\n. Speak privately to the daughter about her sexual activity.\nPerform a vaginal pelvic examination.\n. Commence intravenous fluid resuscitation.\n. Perform urinary beta-hCG pregnancy test.\nArrange for urgent transvaginal ultrasound.\nMOQ >\nMCQ 2.071\nAfter his baby sister was born, a é-year-old boy began sucking his thumb and\nwetting his bed, behaviours he had ‘grown out of'' long before. His behaviour is a\nexample of which one of the following?\nReaction formation.\nRegression.\n. Acting out.\n. Jealousy.\nCompensation.\nMOOR >\nMCQ 2.072\nThis is the photograph of a 17-year-old girl. The swelling\nvisible in her neck has been present for several months,\nis painless and is slowly increasing in size. She has not\nnoticed any voice changes, nor has she experienced\nany difficulty in swallowing or breathing. The lump is not\nattached to the overlying skin and moves on swallowing.\nWhich one of the following is the most likely diagnosis?","options":{"A":"Medullary carcinoma of the thyroid.","B":"Thyroglossal duct cyst.","C":"Papillary carcinoma of the thyroid.","D":"Branchial cyst.","E":"Colloid cyst confined to the thyroid isthmus.\n\nSUE\nMCQ 2.073\n\nA 26-year-old woman (gravida 3, para 2), whose only Papanicolaou (Pap) smear\ntest was done five years ago and was normal, is admitted to hospital at 33 weeks of\ngestation, following an antepartum haemorrhage of 300mL. The bleeding has now\nceased. Vital signs are as follows."},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"medium","currentness_keywords":["pregnan","resuscitation"],"