one of the following human allografts from cadaver donors?','{"A":"Cornea.","B":"Heart.","C":"Kidney.","D":"Pancreas.","E":"Liver.\n\nMCQ 2.075\n\nA 50-year-old man presents with a two-month history of\ndiscomfort in the left side of the scrotum which is worse\nwhen standing. He is otherwise in good health. The\nphotograph illustrates the clinical findings. Which one of the\nfollowing is the most likely diagnosis?\n\nA. Varicocele.\n\nB. Epididymal cyst.\n\nC. Encysted hydrocele of the cord.\nD. Seminoma of the testis.\n\nE. Scrotal hydrocele.\n\nMCQ 2.076\n\nA 25-year-old primigravid patient at 40 weeks of gestation presented because she\nhad not felt any fetal movements for 24 hours. The fetal heart beats were clearly\naudible on auscultation at a rate of 140/min, and the cardiotocograph (CTG) was\nnormal and reactive. Her cervix was 2cm dilated and fully effaced. You therefore\nreassured her and sent her home. She telephones you 24 hours later and tells you\nthat she has still not felt any fetal movements, now for 48 hours. Which one of the\n\nfollowing is the most appropriate next step in management?"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"2.074","duplicate_group_id":"exact-c66ed9dc28be","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"8da2c39e646bf1703e5d","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":85,"source_qid":"2.074"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"8da2c39e646bf1703e5d","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choi