Section 2 — Trial Examination
. Admit for induction of labour.
Immediate Caesarean section.
. Urgent oxytocin challenge test.
. Urgent ultrasound scan of the fetus.
Amniotic fluid volume assessment.
moO >
MCQ 2.077
An 18-year-old student presents with a five-day history of fevers, headaches, sore
throat, malaise, and mild arthralgia of the hands and elbow joints. On examination,
her temperature is 37.7°C, there is ulcerative pharyngitis, a fine maculopapular rash,
generalised lymphadenopathy and a palpable tender spleen. Investigations show
the following results.
White cell count *16.0x109/L (4.0-11.0)
(WCC)
Neutrophils *11.0x10°/L (2.0-7.5)
Lymphocytes *4.5x109/L 1.5-4.0)
The blood film show atypical lymphocytes.
Monospot (Paul-Bunnell) test is negative.
Which one of the following is the most likely diagnosis?','{"A":"Streptococcal infection.","B":"Measles.","C":"Rubella.","D":"Herpes simplex infection.","E":"Infectious mononucleosis.\n\nCee ee a\n\nMCQ 2.078\n\nA 26-year-old woman at 36 weeks of gestation in her first pregnancy presents\nbecause of headache and right-sided upper abdominal pain of two days duration.\nThe pregnancy has been normal until now. Her BP is 145/90mmHg, her ankles are\nslightly swollen and urinalysis shows protein ++. There is some tenderness under\nthe right costal margin. Which one of the following is the most likely cause of her\nsymptoms and examination findings?\n\nA.\nB.\n€\nD\nEF\n\nChronic renal disease.\nBiliary cholestasis.\n. Pre-eclampsia.\n. Cholecystitis.\nAcute fatty liver of pregnancy."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"2.077","duplicate_group_id":"exact-a59de81f53dc","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"5fbf015fb44a4127ee8e","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":86,"source_qid":"2.077"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','low','{"record_id":"5fbf015fb44a4127ee8e","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":86,"source_qid":"2.077","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Ausiralian Medical Council\nSection 2 — Trial Examination\n. Admit for induction of labour.\nImmediate Caesarean section.\n. Urgent oxytocin challenge test.\n. Urgent ultrasound scan of the fetus.\nAmniotic fluid volume assessment.\nmoO >\nMCQ 2.077\nAn 18-year-old student presents with a five-day history of fevers, headaches, sore\nthroat, malaise, and mild arthralgia of the hands and elbow joints. On examination,\nher temperature is 37.7°C, there is ulcerative pharyngitis, a fine maculopapular rash,\ngeneralised lymphadenopathy and a palpable tender spleen. Investigations show\nthe following results.\nWhite cell count *16.0x109/L (4.0-11.0)\n(WCC)\nNeutrophils *11.0x10°/L (2.0-7.5)\nLymphocytes *4.5x109/L 1.5-4.0)\nThe blood film show atypical lymphocytes.\nMonospot (Paul-Bunnell) test is negative.\nWhich one of the following is the most likely diagnosis?","options":{"A":"Streptococcal infection.","B":"Measles.","C":"Rubella.","D":"Herpes simplex infection.","E":"Infectious mononucleosis.\n\nCee ee a\n\nMCQ 2.078\n\nA 26-year-old woman at 36 weeks of gestation in her first pregnancy presents\nbecause of headache and right-sided upper abdominal pain of two days duration.\nThe pregnancy has been normal until now. Her BP is 145/90mmHg, her ankles are\nslightly swollen and urinalysis shows protein ++. There is some tenderness under\nthe right costal margin. Which one of the following is the most likely cause of her\nsymptoms and examination findings?\n\nA.\nB.\n€\nD\nEF\n\nChronic renal disease.\nBiliary cholestasis.\n. Pre-eclampsia.\n. Cholecystitis.\nAcute fatty liver of pregnancy."},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"low","currentness_keywords":[],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"a59de81f53dc7da234d655f1be7f120f409acc52","duplicate_group_id":"exact-a59de81f53dc","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"5fbf015fb44a4127ee8e","record_type":"text