Section 2 = Trial Examination _
MCQ 2.079
Which one of the following would be most in keeping with an obstructing stone in
the (common) bile duct?
Urobilinogen in the urine, no bilirubin in the urine.
Urobilinogen in the urine, bilirubin in the urine.
. Conjugated hyperbilirubinaemia, bilirubin in the urine, no urinary urobilinogen.
. A high ratio of unconjugated to conjugated bilirubin in the serum.
High levels of conjugated bilirubin and transaminases in the serum, urinary
urobilinogen increased.
ih (eo). () ees
MCQ 2.080
Clinical features of schizophrenia may include thought disorder, spontaneous
remission, negative symptoms, poor response to medication and persecutory
delusions. In contrast to early onset schizophrenia, which one of these clinical
features is most likely to occur in late onset schizophrenia (schizophrenia beginning
for the first time after the age of 45 years)?','{"A":"Negative symptoms.","B":"Thought disorder.","C":"Persecutory delusions.","D":"Spontaneous remission.","E":"Poor response to medication.\n\nMCQ 2.081\n\nA 3-year-old girl has had fever and swelling of her right eye for 24 hours. On\nexamination, she looks unwell, has a fever of 38.8°C, right periorbital oedema, with\nswollen erythematous eyelids. Extraocular eye movements are full with no evidence\nof chemosis or proptosis. She has no neck stiffness. Which one of the following is the\nmost appropriate next step in management?\n\n. Urgent computed tomography (CT) of orbital fossae.\nLumbar puncture.\n\n. Topical chloramphenicol ointment.\n\n. Oral prednisolone and antihistamines.\nIntravenous flucloxacillin and ceftriaxone.\n\nMOQ >"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"2.079","duplicate_group_id":"exact-bdc9d8f8df55","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"3ec856b7b4861a1d60e1","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":87,"source_qid":"2.079"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"3ec856b7b4861a1d60e1","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":87,"source_qid":"2.079","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Australian Medical Council\nSection 2 = Trial Examination _\nMCQ 2.079\nWhich one of the following would be most in keeping with an obstructing stone in\nthe (common) bile duct?\nUrobilinoge