t likely cause for these symptoms and results?\n\nA. Acute fatty liver of pregnancy.\n\nB. Obstetric cholestasis.\n\nC. Pre-eclampsia.\n\nD. Cholelithiasis.\n\nE, Viral hepatitis A.\n2 EEEEEEeEemed\n\nMCQ 2.087\n\nA 35-year-old man is seen in general practice. He has fever, a rash all over his body,\nand headaches. His 7-year-old son had chickenpox two weeks ago.\n\nYou diagnose that he has chickenpox (varicella/varicella-zoster virus infection). He\nis concerned about his wife who is 12 weeks pregnant. Which one of the following is\nthe most appropriate first step in management for his wife?\n\nCommence her on aciclovir orally.\n\nCommence her on varicella-zoster virus (VZV) immunoglobulin.\n\n. Wait and watch, since all available drugs could be teratogenic.\n\nCommence her on famciclovir orally.\n\nArrange serum antibodies for varicella-zoster virus (VZV) to check her immunity.\n\nTTMOQ2>"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"low","currentness_keywords":[],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"7f4f74436cd7c12bf7340898f27bb0b9870833d8","duplicate_group_id":"exact-7f4f74436cd7","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"34632a13fb371f63ed91","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":89,"source_qid":"2.085"}]}',0,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source