Section 2 — Trial Examination
A 26-year-old woman presents to the Emergency Department of the local hospita
because she is feeling unwell. Her last menstrual period occurred eight weeks ago
— she usually has periods every month = and she bled heavily vaginally yesterday
The bleeding has been less today. She looks unwell, her pulse rate is 130/min, BP
110/60mmbg, and her temperature is 39.5°C. On abdominal examination she has
suprapubic tenderness and guarding, but no evidence of a pelvic mass. Speculum
examination shows the cervix is open with apparent products of conception in
the upper vagina. Which one of the following is the most appropriate next step in
managment?
Curettage.
Administration of ergometrine.
. Curettage after twelve hours of antibiotic therapy.
Cervical swabs for microscopic assessment and culture.
Antibiotic administration.
MOORP>
MCQ 2.089
A 25-year-old man presents with a
two-month history of intermittent purulent |
discharge in his perineal region. He is |
otherwise in good health and has no |
other symptoms. His past medical history }
is unremarkable and he is not on any
medications. The photograph shows the
clinical findings. The anus is on the lower
aspect of the picture.
