Section 2 - Trial Examination','{"A":"Along-standing brachial plexus injury.","B":"A tumour at the apex of the lung.","C":"Adissecting carotid aneurysm.","D":"Cluster migraine.\n\n£. Aneoplasm in the middle cranial fossa.","E":"Ua antan ESE SESE Enna aan\n\nMCQ 2.094\n\nA 25-year-old man presents with a painless, left-sided scrotal swelling which has been\npresent for three weeks. Examination shows a tense hydrocele. The underlying testis\nis impalpable. Which one of the following is the most appropriate next investigation?\n\nHydrocele aspiration and palpation of the left testis.\nUltrasound examination of the left testis.\n\n. Computed tomography (CT) of the abdomen and chest.\n. Beta-hCG and alpha fetoprotein estimations.\nIntravenous urography.\n\nMOO >\n\nMCQ 2.095\n\nA 60-year-old man presents with a very painful swollen right knee developing over\nthe past two days. There is no history of trauma.\n\nHis vital signs are normal. He has a painful tender knee effusion, with a fever of\nsey\n\nHe drinks five to six cans of beer daily and smokes 10 cigarettes daily. He has\nhypertension and is on hydrochlorothiazide 25mg daily and metoprolol 100mg daily.\n\nHis full blood count, electrolytes and urea are within normal limits. Joint aspiration\nshows clear fluid with negative birefringent crystals on microscopy.\n\nWhich one of the following medications is the most appropriate immediate\nmanagement?\n\n_A\n\nA lopurinol.\nB. Colchicine.\nC. Indomethacin.\nD. Prednisolone.\nE. Paracetamol.\n\nMCQ 2.096\n\nA 27-year-old woman undergoes a laparoscopic appendicectomy for perforated\nappendicitis. About 200mL of frank pus is found in the pelvis and washed out.\nThe patient is given a five-day course of antibiotics (gentamicin, amoxycillin and\nmetronidazole). Her postoperative recovery is delayed by a paralytic ileus. Seven\ndays after the procedure she spikes a fever of 39.0°C and develops mucous\ndiarrhoea persisting over the next three days. Which one of the following would be\nthe most likely explanation of her current problem?"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":"2.094","duplicate_group_id":"exact-856af1f20032","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"f5f52e78a55b3ebdb7fd","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":93,"source_qid":"2.094"}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','low','{"record_id":"f5f52e78a55b3ebdb7fd","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":93,"source_qid":"2.094","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Australian Medical Council\nSection 2 - Trial Examination","options":{"A":"Along-standing brachial plexus injury.","B":"A tumour at the apex of the lung.","C":"Adissecting carotid aneurysm.","D":"Cluster migraine.\n\n£. Aneoplasm in the middle cranial fossa.","E":"Ua antan ESE SESE Enna aan\n\nMCQ 2.094\n\nA 25-year-old man presents with a painless, left-sided scrotal swelling which has been\npresent for three weeks. Examination shows a tense hydrocele. The underlying testis\nis impalpable. Which one of the following is the most appropriate next investigation?\n\nHydrocele aspiration and palpation of the left testis.\nUltrasound examination of the left testis.\n\n. Computed tomography (CT) of the abdomen and chest.\n. Beta-hCG and alpha fetoprotein estimations.\nIntravenous urography.\n\nMOO >\n\nMCQ 2.095\n\nA 60-year-old man presents with a very painful swollen right knee developing over\nthe past two days. There is no history of trauma.\n\nHis vital signs are normal. He has a painful tender knee effusion, with a fever of\nsey\n\nHe drinks five to six cans of beer daily and smokes 10 cigarettes daily. He has\nhypertension and is on hydrochlorothiazide 25mg daily and metoprolol 100mg daily.\n\nHis full blood count, electrolytes and urea are within normal limits. Joint aspiration\nshows clear fluid with negative birefringent crystals on microscopy.\n\nWhich one of the following medications is the most appropriate immediate\nmanagement?\n\n_A\n\nA lopurinol.\nB. Colchicine.\nC. Indomethacin.\nD. Prednisolone.\nE. Paracetamol.\n\nMCQ 2.096\n\nA 27-year-old woman undergoes a laparoscopic appendicectomy for perforated\nappendicitis. About 200mL of frank pus is found in the pelvis and washed out.\nThe patient is given a five-day course of antibiotics (gentamicin, amoxycillin and\nmetronidazole). Her postoperative recovery is delayed by a paralytic ileus. Seven\ndays after the procedure she spikes a fever of 39.0°C and develops mucous\ndiarrhoea persisting over the next three days. Which one of the following would be\nthe most likely explanation of her current problem?"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"low","currentness_keywords":[],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"856af1f200320f5f452a6dde178bcfa75a0d96ef","duplicate_group_id":"exact-856af1f20032","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"f5f52e78a55b3ebdb7fd","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":93,"source_qid":"2.094"}]}',0,'v2.9.4','2026-09-