Section 2 - Trial Examination
MCQ 2.109
A 60-year-old man presents to the Emergency Department after vomiting ¢
large amount of fresh blood. He is normally in good health and apart from some
indigestion after meals, has never had anything like this before. He drinks the
equivalent of 30g alcohol a day and is not on any medications. Which one of the
following is the most likely cause of the bleeding?
Oesophagitis.
Gastric ulcer.
. Gastric carcinoma.
Mallory-Weiss syndrome.
Duodenal ulcer.
—_—_—_—COCOOCCC: eee
MCQ 2.110
FOC) 1S
