Section 2 - Trial Examination
A. Computed tomographic (CT) venography of the leg.
B. Conventional contrast venography of the leg.
C. D-dimer assay.
D. Duplex Doppler ultrasound studies of the lower limb.
E. Magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) of the leg.
eee SSeS
MCQ 2.113
A 26-year-old recently married woman, who has always had very irregular mensirual
cycles varying between four and ten weeks duration, returns to the clinic one
week after her previous routine review. At that time she indicated her last period
had occurred six weeks previously. The results of the tests you arranged then are as
follows:
Serum follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH) 3 IU/L (<13)
Serum luteinising hormone (LH) *850 IU/L (4-10 in follicular phase, 20-100
at mid-cycle)
Serum prolactin (PRL) A75mU/L (50-500)
Which one of the following is the most likely cause of her continuing amenorrhoea?
A. Stress from her recent marriage.
B. Polycystic ovarian syndrome (PCOS).
C. Premature ovarian failure.
D. Early pregnancy.
E. An LH-producing pituitary adenoma.
secoossssunanansssssenssnsennesensseetetasnsssnssnsanessssesessssesesssessessessssssssaassssstesssssssasssssssssssssstttttssetsssiessssSsssSstsssesissneaseeset
MCQ 2.114
Carcinoma of the breast is discovered at 22 weeks of gestation in the second
pregnancy of a 32-year-old woman. The tumour is 1.5cm in size, is located in the
upper outer quadrant of the left breast, and produces dimpling of the overlying
skin. A core biopsy has confirmed invasive ductal carcinoma. There are no clinically
suspicious axillary nodes and no evidence of metastases on physical examination
or chest imaging. Blood chemistry is normal. Which one of the following is the most
appropriate approach to the treatment of this patient?','{"A":"Treatment should be delayed until the baby is delivered at term.","B":"The pregnancy should be terminated and a mastectomy performed two months\nlater.","C":"The patient should proceed to definitive surgery.","D":"Preliminary local irradiation therapy should be followed by definitive surgery after\ndelivery.","E":"Before consideration of mastectomy or other treatment, the response to\noophorectomy should be determined.\n83"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","supporting_pages":[99],"source_qid":"2.113","duplicate_group_id":"exact-246de8436ce1","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"e4b49bd17e57920b4c4b","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":99,"source_qid":"2.113"}],"parser_version":"2.8-residual-resolver-selective-ocr-visual-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v28_selective_ocr_multi_group","text_method":"v28_selective_ocr","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,'text',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"e4b49bd17e57920b4c4b","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_year":null,"source_page":99,"supporting_pages":[99],"source_qid":"2.113","domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Australian Medical Council\nSection 2 - Trial Examination\nA. Computed tomographic (CT) venography of the leg.\nB. Conventional contrast venography of the leg.\nC. D-dimer assay.\nD. Duplex Doppler ultrasound studies of the lower limb.\nE. Magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) of the leg.\neee SSeS\nMCQ 2.113\nA 26-year-old recently married woman, who has always had very irregular mensirual\ncycles varying between four and t