uced somatic delusion.\nC. Factitious disorder.\n\nD. Body dysmorphism.\n\nE. Perceptual disturbance.\n\nMCQ 2.123\n\nA 70-year-old woman presents with weight loss of 3kg, vague headaches, aching all |\nover the body and morning stiffness of the shoulder and hip girdles. These symptoms\nhave been present for the past six months. Physical examination is normal, except for |\nsome tenderness in the muscles of her shoulder. Investigations show a normochromic |\nnormocytic. anaemia, erythrocyte sedimentation rate (ESR) of 65 mm/h (5-20) and\nraised C-reactive protein. All other investigations, including muscle enzymes, are\nnormal. Which one of the following is the most likely diagnosis?\n\n. Multiple myeloma.\nPolymyalgia rheumatica.\n. Rheumatoid arthritis.\nOccult malignancy.\nPolymyositis.\n\n=\n\nMOQORP>"},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"low","currentness_keywords":[],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"c71bae9ee4024135f3ff46e808c2c6259b77664f","duplicate_group_id":"exact-c71bae9ee402","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"82d58e22ed4f31bb997b","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_relative_path":"96.Handbook of Multiple Choice Questions (Vernon Marshall).pdf","source_page":102,"source_qid":"2.121"}]}',0,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,visual_asset=excluded.visual_ass